Android port: better Auto light and wavelet noise reduction.

* `develop.auto` (pipeline/src/auto.rs): the Exposure still follows the calibrated rule on the scene's
  log-average luminance, but Highlights, Whites, Shadows, Blacks, Contrast and Vibrance now adapt to the
  picture (clipping headroom, share of deep shadows, tonal range, colourfulness) within bounds, instead of
  being fixed numbers.
* Noise reduction (pipeline/src/nr.rs, local.rs): a stationary wavelet (a trous) shrinkage with a noise level
  measured from the picture itself replaces the guided filter and the chromaticity blur. Luminance is
  cleaned in the log luminance, colour noise in the log chromaticity with more levels.
* The GPU render (gpu/src/render.rs) reads the picture back for the noise reduction stage when it is on
  and filters it on the CPU (the filter exists on the CPU only).
